{#
  The photos view (FSD §8.3). One picture, edge to edge — the panel shows
  2560×1440 exactly 1:1, so the layout may bleed to the border.

  This template is deliberately pointless work: the cached crop could be pushed
  to the display without ever touching Chromium. It goes through the template
  anyway, because the purpose of phase 3 is to prove *this whole path*, not to
  get a photo onto the wall (entwicklungsprozess.md §8).

  The image comes in through a file:// URL from the media tree and is already
  exactly 2560×1440; ``object-fit: cover`` is only insurance against a cached
  crop from an older format.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>{{ photo_name }}</title>
    <style>
      html,
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        overflow: hidden;
        /* Black, so a failed image load is unmistakable rather than a subtle
           off-white that could pass for a bright photo. */
        background: #000;
      }
      img {
        display: block;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        object-fit: cover;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <img src="{{ photo_url }}" alt="" />
  </body>
</html>
